{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1015","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1015","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1015\",\"parent_revision\":\"218d9c6aed6340dc6c94a9d9ee6406115ca92ee982373834965df56380d867a9\",\"root_revision\":\"218d9c6aed6340dc6c94a9d9ee6406115ca92ee982373834965df56380d867a9\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe backlog_list MCP tool returns items but provides no indication of GitHub backend status or issue counts. After the migration to ~/.dh/projects/{slug}/, the first call with an empty local cache returns 0 items with no signal that GitHub sync is needed. The tool should include a status footer showing backend availability and counts. Format: `Backend: GitHub, Backend availability: reachable, Backend items (178 open / 245 total)` when GitHub is accessible, or `Backend: GitHub, Backend availability: Needs Authentication, Backend items (--- open / --- total)[cache: 199 open / 300 total]` when GitHub is unavailable and showing cached data.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Claims checked**: 4\\n**VERIFIED**: 2 | **REFUTED**: 0 | **INCONCLUSIVE**: 2\\n\\n### Claim 1: \\\"backlog_list returns items but provides no indication of GitHub backend status\\\"\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED\\n**Evidence**: File: `backlog_core/server.py:269-278` \u2014 Return dict is `{**result, \\\"items\\\": page_items, \\\"count\\\": len(page_items), \\\"pagination\\\": pagination, **out.to_dict()}`. No backend, availability, or status fields present.\\n\\n### Claim 2: \\\"After migration to ~/.dh/projects/{slug}/, first call with empty local cache returns 0 items with no signal\\\"\\n**Verdict**: INCONCLUSIVE\\n**Evidence**: `dh_paths.py:76-160` confirms migration structure. `backlog_list` accepts `from_github: bool = False` and only syncs when explicitly requested. Empty-cache behavior is parameter-driven, not automatic.\\n\\n### Claim 3: \\\"The tool should include a status footer\\\"\\n**Verdict**: INCONCLUSIVE\\n**Evidence**: MCP tools return JSON dicts, not text footers. The proposal format is human-readable text. Implementation should use a new dict key (e.g., `backend_status`) with structured fields, not literal text.\\n\\n### Claim 4: \\\"GitHub API availability patterns\\\"\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED\\n**Evidence**: `backlog_core/github.py:1043-1065` \u2014 Uses PyGitHub, `GITHUB_TOKEN` env var for auth, raises `GitHubUnavailableError` if not set. `try_get_github()` returns None on failure for fallback to local-only.\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: backlog_list should show GitHub availability status and issue counts\\nGoal: Add a backend status dict to backlog_list MCP tool output\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Location of backlog_list implementation | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: backlog_core/server.py:269-278\\n2. Current backlog_list return schema | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Returns {items, count, pagination, messages, warnings} \u2014 no backend fields\\n3. GitHub API method for availability and counts | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: github.py has try_get_github(), GitHubUnavailableError, PyGithub repo.open_issues_count\\n4. Desired output format | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Note: Clarified from text footer to structured backend dict\\n5. How backlog_list accesses GitHub | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: from_github param triggers refresh_local_cache_from_github() via PyGithub\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Conditions 1,2,3,5: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by fact-checker and impact-analyst)\\n- Condition 4: Remained AVAILABLE, clarified format\\n- No new MISSING conditions discovered\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED \u2014 all 5 conditions AVAILABLE\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **backlog_list should show github availability status and issue counts (open/total)** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: User request \u2014 session 2026-03-22, observed empty backlog_list after DH state migration\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-23)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. Start with empty `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/backlog/` cache (fresh migration or new user)\\n2. Call `backlog_list(from_github=False)` (the default)\\n3. Observe: returns `{\\\"items\\\": [], \\\"count\\\": 0}` with no signal that GitHub sync exists\\n4. User cannot tell if: (a) backlog is actually empty, (b) GitHub is unreachable, or (c) `from_github=True` is needed\\n5. Call `backlog_list(from_github=True)` to refresh from GitHub\\n6. Observe: same return schema, no indication backend was consulted or succeeded\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\nP1 \u2014 Silent failure on first use: new users see empty backlog with zero feedback that sync is needed. Backend state invisible: no way to diagnose \\\"why is my backlog empty?\\\" without re-reading docs. After `.dh/` migration, cache is the primary source \u2014 users need cache freshness and sync signals.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n**Core**: `backlog_core/server.py::backlog_list` (producer), `backlog_core/github.py` (backend), `backlog_core/models.py` (types)\\n**Tests**: `test_backlog_core_server.py` \u2014 structure validation needs update, 2-3 new test paths\\n**Docs**: `backlog/README.md`, `backlog/SKILL.md` \u2014 return schema docs\\n**Agents**: `backlog-mcp-validator.md` \u2014 may need schema update\\n**Downstream**: All callers receive new `backend` dict \u2014 backwards compatible (additive)\\n\\n### Scope\\n\\n**Expected Behavior \u2014 GitHub reachable:**\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"items\\\": [...], \\\"count\\\": 2, \\\"pagination\\\": {...},\\n  \\\"backend\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"GitHub\\\", \\\"availability\\\": \\\"reachable\\\", \\\"open_count\\\": 47, \\\"total_count\\\": 203},\\n  \\\"messages\\\": [...], \\\"warnings\\\": [...]\\n}\\n```\\n**Expected Behavior \u2014 GitHub unavailable:**\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"items\\\": [...], \\\"count\\\": 1, \\\"pagination\\\": {...},\\n  \\\"backend\\\": {\\\"name\\\": \\\"GitHub\\\", \\\"availability\\\": \\\"needs_authentication\\\", \\\"open_count\\\": null, \\\"total_count\\\": null, \\\"cache_open_count\\\": 12, \\\"cache_total_count\\\": 87, \\\"error\\\": \\\"GITHUB_TOKEN not set\\\"},\\n  \\\"messages\\\": [\\\"Using cached data\\\"], \\\"warnings\\\": [\\\"GitHub backend unavailable\\\"]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\\n- [ ] `backlog_list()` returns `backend` dict in response root\\n- [ ] `backend.availability` is one of: \\\"reachable\\\", \\\"needs_authentication\\\", \\\"rate_limited\\\", \\\"error\\\"\\n- [ ] When reachable: `open_count` and `total_count` are live integers from GitHub\\n- [ ] When not reachable: counts are null, `cache_open_count`/`cache_total_count` provided if cache exists\\n- [ ] `backend.error` populated only when not reachable\\n- [ ] Existing return keys (`items`, `count`, `pagination`, `messages`, `warnings`) unchanged\\n- [ ] `test_backlog_list_structure` asserts `backend` key with required fields\\n- [ ] New test for GitHub-unavailable path with cache fallback\\n- [ ] New test for empty cache + unavailable GitHub\\n- [ ] `backlog/README.md` documents `backend` schema with examples\\n- [ ] `backlog/SKILL.md` documents new field\\n- [ ] No breaking changes \u2014 field is additive only\\n- [ ] All code paths return consistent backend structure\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n- `GitHubUnavailableError` in `backlog_core/github.py` \u2014 reuse for error detection\\n- `try_get_github()` \u2014 extend to return error reason\\n- Pydantic models in `models.py` \u2014 use same pattern for BackendStatus\\n- PyGithub `repo.open_issues_count` and `repo.get_issues(state=\\\"all\\\").totalCount` \u2014 cheap queries\\n- Test mocking infrastructure in `test_backlog_core_server.py` \u2014 extend for unavailable paths\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n**Core**: `backlog_core/models.py` (add BackendStatus model), `backlog_core/server.py::backlog_list()` (construct and return backend dict), `backlog_core/github.py` (add safe issue count query method)\\n**Tests**: `tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` (update structure test, add unavailable paths)\\n**Docs**: `skills/backlog/README.md`, `skills/backlog/SKILL.md`\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\nNo new dependencies. Pydantic, PyGitHub already imported. All error handling infrastructure (GitHubUnavailableError, try_get_github) already exists. Test infrastructure in place. No circular dependencies.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- `.claude/agents/backlog-mcp-validator.md` \u2014 If validates backlog_list schema, must expect `backend_status` field\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py::test_backlog_list_structure` \u2014 Verifies presence of keys. Must add `backend_status` to structure validation\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py::test_backlog_list_basic` \u2014 Accesses response items/pagination. Verify new field present\\n- Other test_backlog_list_* functions \u2014 No migration needed, new field is additive\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github.py` \u2014 GitHub access layer (`try_get_github()`, `GitHubUnavailableError`). Will be called to retrieve issue counts\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py` \u2014 Will require new TypedDict or BaseModel for `backend_status` structure\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py::backlog_list` \u2014 Currently returns `{items, count, pagination, messages, warnings}`. Must add `backend_status` dict with: `name` (\\\"GitHub\\\"), `availability` (\\\"reachable\\\"|\\\"Needs Authentication\\\"), `open_count` (int), `total_count` (int), `cache_fallback_used` (bool)\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\nNone identified.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/README.md` \u2014 Section \\\"backlog_list \u2014 List open items\\\" documents return value without backend_status\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/SKILL.md` \u2014 Same section documents tool return schema\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] backlog_list in server.py adds backend_status to all return paths\\n- [ ] Test assertions include backend_status in structure validation\\n- [ ] README.md and SKILL.md document the new footer format\\n- [ ] Validator agent accepts backend_status field\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\nProducers: server.py::backlog_list\\nConsumers: test_backlog_core_server.py (5+ test functions), work-backlog-item SKILL.md, groom-backlog-item SKILL.md, complete-implementation SKILL.md\\nBackend: github.py (GitHub API), models.py (response types)\\nDocs: backlog README.md, backlog SKILL.md\\nAgents: backlog-mcp-validator.md\\nRelated workflows (transparent): milestone skills, group-items-to-milestone, start-milestone, complete-milestone\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:begin -->\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| feature-context | plan/feature-context-backlog-list-github-availability.md | current | feature-researcher | 2026-03-23T21:29:06.305976+00:00 |\\n| codebase